# r7-server: disable ril-daemon. Separate file from
# init.r7-server-vendor-disabled.rc and DELIBERATELY named to sort
# alphabetically after vendor.sem.rilchip.rc.
#
# Why: Android init resolves duplicate `service NAME` definitions by
# letting the LAST-PARSED one that carries `override` win, regardless
# of whether the earlier one also had override. vendor.sem.rilchip.rc's
# own ril-daemon definition already carries `override` (it's designed
# to override a generic AOSP stub), and it sorts after
# "init.r7-server-vendor-disabled.rc" alphabetically - so when
# ril-daemon's disable lived in that file, the real vendor.sem.rilchip.rc
# definition was parsed second and won, silently undoing the override
# (confirmed live 2026-08-13: every other service in that batch was
# correctly suppressed, only ril-daemon stayed running). Every other
# service in the batch file has an original definition WITHOUT
# `override`, so this ordering issue is unique to ril-daemon - a later
# non-override duplicate is simply rejected by init, no naming trick
# needed there.
service ril-daemon /vendor/bin/hw/rild_HYBRIS_DISABLED
    class main
    disabled
    oneshot
    override
